# Black Stride ship definition (.ship format) - the Vanguard-class Cruiser card.
# DESIGN INTENT: a high-end, high-tier cruiser the player earns in the LATE game. The
# starting fleet spawns it today only because it is the sole hull with authored art and
# a hardpoint skeleton; when a proper starter hull card lands, the spawn sites in
# game.cpp move to that id and this card keeps its late-game positioning untouched.
# Art: assets/ships/ships_cruisers_yellow/cruisers_r0_c0.png (394x1586, nose-up).
# At world_scale 1 the hull is 1586 world units long, which classifies it as a
# CRUISER: slow, heavy inertial flight (see ship_size_class_from_length in sim/ship.cpp).
# An explicit `class <drone|corvette|frigate|destroyer|cruiser|capital>` line can override.

id vanguard_cruiser
name "Vanguard-class Cruiser"
desc "Flagship-grade heavy cruiser from the top of the yard's line. A deep hardpoint rack - three medium weapon mounts, twin point-defense rings and a dorsal sensor dome - built for commanders who have outgrown everything else the shipwrights sell."
faction 2
world_scale 1.0
size 394 1586

# ---- Stat card ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# hull: combat entity health at spawn. capacitor: <max> <regen>. motion overrides the
# class tuning table (<max_speed> <accel> <decel> <turn_accel> <max_turn>); these values
# ARE the cruiser table row, authored so the card is explicit about how this hull flies.
# hull/capacitor/motion are still the PARITY baseline, not the hull's final late-game
# statline - retune them here (a data edit) when the hull takes its real place in the
# progression; price/tier already carry the high-end market positioning.
hull 100
capacitor 100 8
motion 240 90 70 1.4 0.45
price 78000
tier 3

layer sprite assets/ships/ships_cruisers_yellow/cruisers_r0_c0.png 0 0 1 0 0

# Box collider matching the art size.
collider -197 -793
collider 197 -793
collider 197 793
collider -197 793

# Hardpoint skeleton: typed module slots pinned to art pixels.
# Format: hardpoint <id> <accepts> <size> <x> <y> <facing_deg> <arc_deg>
# Coords are ship-local art texels (origin = image center, +Y = nose):
#   local_x = pixel_x - 197, local_y = 793 - pixel_y
# facing is CCW from the nose; arc is the mount's total traverse.
hardpoint radar_dome sensor          S    0  643   0 360
hardpoint bow_gun    weapon          M    0  403   0 180
hardpoint port_gun   weapon          M -122 -107  90 210
hardpoint stbd_gun   weapon          M  122 -107 -90 210
hardpoint dorsal_pd  defense         S    0   33   0 360
hardpoint aft_pd     defense         S    0 -387 180 360
hardpoint engine_bay engine          L    0 -687 180   0
hardpoint cargo_bay  utility         M    0 -247   0   0

# Thruster nozzles pinned to art pixels (same texel space as hardpoints; facing is the
# direction the exhaust LEAVES the hull, CCW from the nose; positions measured off the
# sprite's alpha -- the twin stern nozzle blocks sit at px 130-159 / 234-264, exit plane
# ~py 1565). Visual only: ShipRendering projects the flight telemetry onto each nozzle.
# Format: thruster <main|rcs> <x> <y> <facing_deg> [size]
thruster main -52 -772 180 0.55    # port main engine
thruster main  52 -772 180 0.55    # starboard main engine
thruster rcs  -66  523  90 0.8     # bow port lateral (hull edge at row 270)
thruster rcs   66  523 -90 0.8     # bow starboard lateral
thruster rcs  -25  693   0 0.8     # bow port retro (reverse burn, nose flank at row 100)
thruster rcs   25  693   0 0.8     # bow starboard retro
thruster rcs  -75 -577  90 0.8     # stern port lateral (aft skirt at row 1370)
thruster rcs   75 -577 -90 0.8     # stern starboard lateral
